29-## 2. Problem
30-
31:B-f97c removed the immediate failure mode where every `story_review` prompt embedded the complete requirements corpus. That stopgap prevents routine prompt size from scaling with corpus size, but it intentionally does not solve relevant-document discovery.
32-
33-The next problem is recall under a bounded read budget:
34-
35-- deterministic keywords may miss historical synonyms;
36-- one model may reproduce the Story's current wording and miss legacy vocabulary;
37-- model-only search is non-reproducible and may omit exact command, field, or config names;
38-- `relatedDocs` is curated by the owner and cannot be the sole truth source;
39-- a top-N cap without ambiguity handling can hide a relevant document near the cutoff;
40:- reviewer prose cannot prove which files were actually read.
41-
42-## 3. Goals
43-
44-- Keep default full reads bounded without weakening requirement-gap detection.
45-- Combine deterministic recall with independent semantic expansion.
46:- Make every keyword, search query, candidate score, read, omission, and escalation auditable.
47:- Reuse one candidate contract across PLAN scope review, REVIEW behavior/docs lanes, and delivery review without merging their ownership.
48-- Measure recall, precision, token cost, latency, host availability, and escalation frequency.
49-- Fail closed when routing evidence is malformed, stale, ambiguous, or inconsistent with mechanical read logs.
